# dev-profile-incident direnv entry (Phase 5 env plan, section 7).
# Tracked and value-free: directives and non-secret local defaults only.
# Run `direnv allow` once per checkout to opt in (mirrors the `ngc-env-on`
# opt-in philosophy - nothing is exported silently).
#
# What this loads:
# - incident-console/.env.local when present (personal-laptop persistence for
#   the Supabase DSN / R2 keys; absent-by-default stays valid - plain shell
#   exports per LOCAL_MOCK_LOOP.md keep working). Note: incident-console/.env
#   is likewise code-live via config.py's first load_dotenv() call, but direnv
#   only auto-loads .env.local here; export .env values by hand if you use it.
#
# What this NEVER touches:
# - /srv/rise-up/.ngc_env stays manual (`ngc-env-on` in a fresh shell, or
#   `direnv deny` first). Auto-sourcing a shared credential on a shared box
#   would silently arm every shell with someone else's keys.
#
# Footgun: direnv shapes the *invoking shell's* env, and compose
# `environment:` interpolation reads that shell - so a direnv-provided local
# DSN (e.g. SQLite) present in the shell WILL leak into a VM-targeted
# `docker compose --env-file generated.env.*` run from this directory.
# Always deploy from a clean (non-direnv) shell.

dotenv_if_exists incident-console/.env.local

# Non-secret mock-loop defaults (same values as the committed .env template).
export INCIDENT_AGENT_BASE_URL="${INCIDENT_AGENT_BASE_URL:-http://localhost:8000}"
export INCIDENT_LLM_BASE_URL="${INCIDENT_LLM_BASE_URL:-http://localhost:8900/v1}"
